  'storm-damage-roof-repairs': { title: 'SEPARATE THE EVENT FROM THE OBSERVATION.', eyebrow: 'STORM DAMAGE / PRACTICAL NOTES', intro: 'After severe weather, it helps to describe what changed without assuming the source or extent of the change.', signs: 'Look from a safe position for displaced material, fallen debris, new marks, loose-looking edges or water appearing indoors.', context: 'Wind and rain may affect exposed roof and drainage details differently. Safety and access should guide what is observed.', nextStep: 'If you notice an urgent safety concern, avoid the area; otherwise, share the visible change and the weather event in an enquiry.', guide: '/news/roof-leak-inspection/', guideLabel: 'Read the guide to a roof leak inspection' },
