const roofFlashingExplained = `<article class="compact-information news-article"><div class="narrow"><p class="eyebrow">ROOF REPAIR GUIDE / PERTH</p><h1>ROOF FLASHING EXPLAINED.</h1><p>Roof flashing is a weatherproofing detail used where roof materials meet a wall, opening, penetration or change in direction. It helps manage water at a junction; it is not a stand-alone diagnosis or a universal repair method.</p><section><h2>WHAT ROOF FLASHING DOES AT A JUNCTION.</h2><p>Flashing may be visible near roof-to-wall lines, chimneys, skylights, pipes, valleys or transitions between tile and metal roofing. The surrounding materials and the direction water travels are part of the same roofline context. A stain, lifted edge or old sealant at one point does not identify the path of water through every layer.</p></section><section><h2>WHAT YOU CAN SAFELY NOTE.</h2><ul><li>Identify the nearby feature, such as a wall, chimney, skylight, pipe penetration, valley or roof edge.</li><li>Record visible separation, corrosion, staining, debris or water appearing after rain without touching the roof detail.</li><li>Note the adjoining roof material and whether an interior mark or drip appears to relate to the same area.</li></ul></section><section><h2>WHEN A FLASHING DETAIL NEEDS A PROFESSIONAL REPAIR DISCUSSION.</h2><p>If a roof junction appears changed, leaks near an adjoining feature, or has recurring water-related symptoms, the relevant service is <a href="/flashing-repairs/">roof valleys and flashing repairs in Perth</a>. That service page explains the repair enquiry context; the correct scope depends on the actual junction, roof material, drainage route and access conditions.</p><p>Where water is visible indoors, it can also help to read the <a href="/roof-leak-repairs/">roof leak repairs information</a> before making contact. Use safe ground-level photos where they genuinely show the location, and do not climb onto a roof or enter an unsafe roof space to investigate.</p></section><section><h2>MAKE A CLEAR ENQUIRY.</h2><p>Include the property suburb, the feature beside the observation, the roof material where known, what changed and the weather conditions in which it was noticed. Contact us to arrange an on-site assessment, identify the cause and confirm the repair plan and quote.</p><p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Make a roof repair enquiry</a></p></section></div></article>`;
